-- question_in_lambda at 11:11, 15:6 and 19:13: `_` lifts the whole call
-- into a lambda (§6.7), and §8 desugars pipes before placeholders, so the
-- operand a pipe supplies is an argument of that call and sits inside the
-- lambda too. `|>` inserts it FIRST and `<|` last, so the three definitions
-- differ only in where that argument sits and must report the same thing.
g a b = a + b


direct x = g _ (x?)


piped x = x? |> g _


pipedLeft x = g _ <| x?
